{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And also on the road.</b> The fool, in all his doings and words, reveals his lack of sense and knowledge, even when he walks on the road — as though he proclaims upon himself and displays his shame and makes known his deficiency to everyone. And this is the meaning of 'says to everyone that he is a fool': it is as though in his mouth he says to everyone that he is a fool."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:48.919347784Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}